<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asameni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asameni was a trader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akwamu">Akwamu</a> kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> who in 1693 led a party posing as customers that seized the Danish fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osu-castle">Christiansborg</a> at Osu, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a>. He held it for about a year, flying his own flag and trading with European ships, before selling it back to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in 1694 while keeping its keys, which Akwamu still holds.</p></div>
